<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">The translation layer</span>
    <h2>You describe it. Your agent writes it.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      With the KILN skill (Claude) or the MCP server (any agent), your AI agent becomes the modeller
      between what you want and the models your game loads.
    </p>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li class="box">
        <span class="who">You <small>English</small></span>
        <p class="say">"A bean pilot for my airline game. Waddles, waves."</p>
      </li>
      <li class="box">
        <span class="who">Agent <small>Claude + KILN skill / MCP</small></span>
        <ul>
          <li>plans it in metres, writes <code>pilot.kiln.yaml</code></li>
          <li>runs <code>kiln lint</code></li>
          <li>looks at the turntable</li>
          <li>fixes what's off</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="box">
        <span class="who">KILN <small>the kiln</small></span>
        <ul>
          <li>meshes and paints it</li>
          <li>rigs and animates it</li>
          <li>applies the style</li>
          <li>deterministic builds</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="box game">
        <span class="who">Your game <small>any engine</small></span>
        <ul class="files">
          <li>pilot.glb</li>
          <li>pilot.tscn</li>
          <li>manifest.json</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

